{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/johnsonShortestPaths(weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"johnsonShortestPaths","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13ShortestPaths14DistanceMatrixV","text":"DistanceMatrix","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DistanceMatrix"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","text":"AdditiveArithmetic","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Weights may be negative. Bellman–Ford from a virtual source joined to every vertex gives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" a potential h(v), and Dijkstra’s algorithm runs from every vertex over the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reduced weights h(u) + w - h(v), which are nonnegative. Parallel edges count by their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cheapest. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findNegativeCycle(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a negative cycle when this is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". On sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graphs this is faster than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floydWarshallShortestPaths(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(nm) for Bellman–Ford in the worst case (about one pass when no weight is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"negative), then O(n · (n + m) log n); O(n²) space.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No weight is NaN; every sum fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":", the reduced weights and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reduced distances included. With floating point, distances are converted back from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reduced ones and can differ from Floyd–Warshall’s by rounding."}]}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/jo